+**Pseudocode**
+```python
+def map_reconstruction(P, R, lambda_val, max_iter=100, tol=1e-6):
+    # Initialize object estimate and iteration counter [G]
+    f = zeros_like(P) # Placeholder for object size N
+    k = 0
+    while k < max_iter:
+        # Compute forward projection and residual [G]
+        proj_est = R @ f
+        residual = P - proj_est
+        # Compute gradient of data fidelity term [G]
+        grad_J1 = -2 * R.T @ residual
+        # Compute gradient of prior fidelity term J2(f) [G]
+        grad_J2 = compute_prior_gradient(f)
+        # Compute combined gradient [G]
+        grad_J = grad_J1 + lambda_val * grad_J2
+        # Update estimate using optimizer (GC or EM) [S2, unofficial]
+        f = update_step(f, grad_J, k)
+        # Check convergence criteria [G]
+        if norm(grad_J) < tol:
+            break
+        k += 1
+    return f
+```
